# fastchess auto-writes config.json to its cwd on every run; the runbook
# convention is to invoke scripts/match.sh from REPO_ROOT, so the file lands
# at REPO_ROOT/config.json. (Other cwds either fall under /target or land
# outside the repo entirely and don't need a gitignore rule.)
/config.json

# M6.G/M6.H/M6.H2 corpus-lane bytes: gitignored (operator-materialized via
# re-run.sh from the manifest's pinned knobs + on-demand `corpus fetch` of
# CCRL / Lichess sources). The committed manifest + filter_spec + the vendored
# opening book are sufficient for byte-identical reproduction; the bytes
# themselves can grow to hundreds of MB (self-play) or low GB once fetch pulls
# in external PGN sources, all without meaningful git delta, so we don't track
# them. M6.H2: each lane lives in its own dir under bench/corpus/ and produces
# one flat `lane.bin` (no train/val split — that moves to M6.I). Future hosting
# (GitHub release asset / S3 / sister-repo) will let consumers download a
# frozen canonical artifact instead of re-running re-run.sh. See ADR-0035 §8/§12.
/bench/corpus/**/lane.bin
/bench/corpus/**/checkpoint.bin
# M6.H per-URL fetch bookkeeping (bytes/positions/terminated per source URL).
/bench/corpus/fetch-state.json
# Per-game staging files (one per worker-completed game, consumed and
# unlinked by the dedup thread in strict game_id order). Holds at most
# ~K files at any time during a running campaign; empty when the
# consumer has caught up. See ADR-0035 §3.5 (per-game-file reorder).
/bench/corpus/**/pending/
# Per-spill / per-stage operator artifacts.
/target/corpus-raw/
/target/corpus-spill/
/target/corpus-work/
/target/corpus-campaign.log
